+# OffMenu managed Gitflow
+
+The original helper at `ae7f1a5a2e44a857c2683adf32180e821c0bfd54`
+was a preserved foundation implementation exception from cached main. Its
+independent review and prior task history remain retained. The current audit
+uses `feature/autonomous-gitflow-review-20261014`, freshly based on develop
+`abe0ddc9db357b1e8d0d61825392d6b9923352f0` in the same Worker09 path.
+The helper source is carried by immutable reference from the reviewed original;
+that does not retroactively qualify its old task base or certify a release.
+A preserved capture-ref incident was repaired separately by its owner; this
+helper neither repairs nor bypasses auxiliary refs. Use actual receipts for
+current fetch, review, acceptance and custody status.
+
+The fixed local pool is 32 permanent worker paths. Do not provision an extra
+worker/worktree/session for task dispatch. An idle checkout is a provisioning
+snapshot, not proof of task freshness. Mandatory `auto_review` remains in force;
+it is not evidence of a separately configured approval policy.
+
+## Routine autonomous delivery authority
+
+Matt authorizes the normal qualified OffMenu Gitflow lifecycle: routine reviewed
+PR-to-develop delivery, certification-gated main promotion and immutable tag,
+release fixes back to persistent develop, and reviewed hotfixes from freshly
+fetched released main back to both lines. Do not ask again for routine actions
+inside that standing authority. Product START, production deployment, paid
+sources, credentials and mandatory platform/security confirmations remain
+separate. This authority changes no GitHub protection, setting or Action.
+The previous blanket ledger gate requiring a fresh human approval for every
+routine PR is superseded by this explicit instruction; preserve its history.
+
+Use the existing native fixed pool under direct Morgan ownership. Observed
+checkout behavior is a registered permanent Git worktree and a normal unique
+feature branch created from a successful locked develop fetch in the same path.
+Do not infer Symfony, Linear or scheduler behavior. No app handoff was performed
+or verified here; Git checkout does not prove app-level handoff. No scheduler,
+coordinator or additional worker is installed by this workflow.
+
+The sequence is immutable candidate -> independent exact review -> corrections
+and re-review -> Morgan verdict -> normal PR to develop -> exact live head/base
+and platform checks -> normal merge -> durable merge/custody receipt -> safe
+retirement -> fresh assignment. Never self-accept. A prior task receipt must pin
+its branch/HEAD, tracked/staged/untracked and ignored custody, symlinks/owners,
+immutable outputs and pending review/integration state before reuse. An explicit
+new assignment may preserve and defer the old branch; it does not fabricate old
+acceptance or grant cleanup. Delete no permanent checkout and preserve retained
+reports and dependency symlinks.
+
+### Routine preflight helper
+
+`delivery --worker N --snapshot LIVE_SNAPSHOT_JSON --head FULL_SHA --base FULL_SHA`
+uses the same common global options as other commands. It does not create a PR,
+push or merge. Policy `routine_delivery` pins `authorizer: Matt`, `project: OffMenu`,
+`scope: normal-qualified-gitflow` and an actual standing-authority evidence
+reference. Policy `reviews` must contain an exact `deliver-develop` Morgan verdict
+for candidate/head, base and source/head; a release tag is not a prerequisite for
+ordinary reviewed development integration. Ordinary dispatch can use
+`routine_develop` with Morgan `reviewed-integration-line`, the exact freshly fetched
+SHA and preserved line evidence; this does not certify a release. Existing
+release promotion, tags, main/hotfix and backmerge qualifications remain enforced.
+
+The live snapshot must include explicit `security_alerts`. Any known alert also
+requires `security_confirmation` with confirmed exact head/base and actual
+disposition evidence, separate from platform or routine authority. A stale or
+missing disposition blocks; the helper never dismisses a scanner finding.
+
+The live snapshot must have `state: open`, `base_ref: develop`, `head_ref`, exact
+`head` and `base`, owner and URL. `independent_review` pins distinct reviewer,
+`state: passed`, exact head/base and actual evidence. `requirements_status: known`
+and explicit `required_reviews`, `required_checks`, `advisory_reviews` inventories
+are required. Required reviews must be APPROVED at that head; required checks
+completed/success at that head. Unknown requirements without explicit client authority, stale evidence or pending
+required gates block. Matt explicitly accepts client-side enforcement because
+private origin entitlement/managed-app Administration access does not support
+server protection inspection/enforcement. Keep origin private and do not upgrade
+or add admin credentials. With snapshot `requirements_status:
+origin-unavailable-client-enforced` and policy `client_enforcement` containing
+`accepted_by: Matt`, `origin_protection: unavailable`,
+`bypassable_outside_workflow: true` and an actual evidence reference, unavailable
+origin protection does not hold delivery. Explicit client required-review/check
+inventories and platform/security confirmation still apply; never label origin
+protected or silently invent origin requirements. Advisory pending state is disclosed in the receipt and is
+not substituted for approval. Every advisory entry records `open_findings`; known
+findings require ordinary corrections and fresh review. `platform_confirmation`
+must explicitly record confirmed head/base plus actual evidence. Do not synthesize
+that confirmation from standing authority or infer requirements from an empty API
+result. Snapshot records/evidence remain trusted Morgan custody, not independently
+authenticated signatures or automatic API collection.
+
+The helper reads the live branch head and freshly fetches develop under the
+shared flock. A changed head or base invalidates the candidate. Before invoking
+the normal provider merge, re-read exact PR head/base and pass the expected head
+to the provider; serialize Morgan's develop deliveries. This is a local preflight,
+not an atomic server base lock or branch protection. Verify the normal merge's
+parents/tree afterward against approved head/base, fetch canonical develop and
+retain API and Git receipts. A mismatch is an incident and blocks retirement;
+never reset a public merge to hide it. A normal merge receipt does not certify a
+release. App/API mandatory confirmation cannot be bypassed by helper output.
