+### Per-worker launch and normal merge receipts
+
+From the existing permanent worker path, use
+`python3 -B /path/to/reviewed/scripts/offmenu-gitflow-launch.py --policy POLICY
+--evidence-dir RECEIPTS delivery --snapshot SNAPSHOT --head SHA --base SHA`.
+The launcher derives worker01–32 from the current path, refuses repo/worker
+argument overrides, strips inherited Git variables and delegates one command.
+It creates no scheduler or owner handoff. Common-dir/origin/path/custody validation
+remains in the helper. Existing hooks were inventoried read-only; no existing
+hook was overwritten, disabled or installed by this change. This is explicit
+managed invocation, and all client controls are bypassable outside the workflow.
+Pool-wide activation is not inferred from this Worker09 source commit.
+
+After a normal provider merge, `merge_receipt --worker N --snapshot MERGED_JSON
+--preflight EXACT_ALLOWED_DELIVERY_RECEIPT` verifies the actual pre-merge gate,
+PR URL/head/base, normal merged state, provider evidence and merge UTC. Posthoc
+approval is refused. It freshly fetches canonical develop and verifies merge
+ancestry, exactly ordered base/head parents and the approved candidate tree.
+A differing merge blocks cleanup and retains evidence; no force/reset repair.
+The merged JSON carries `state: merged`, `base_ref: develop`, `url`, `head`, `base`,
+`merge_sha`, `normal_merge: true`, `merged_at`, and `provider_evidence` file reference.
+This receipt establishes integration, not release certification or retirement.
+Continue explicit owner/dirty/untracked/ignored/PR/dependency checks, preserve the
+immutable history, then obtain the next fresh assignment. Release/main/tag and
+released-main hotfix controls remain certification/review gated as above; no real
+main/release action or deployment was performed by this audit.
