+### Dispatch
+
+```sh
+python3 -B scripts/offmenu-gitflow.py --repo /home/user/src/offmenu-workers/worker-09 \
+  --policy /absolute/retained/policy.json --evidence-dir /absolute/retained/receipts \
+  start --worker 9 --kind feature --task unique-task-20261014 --check-only
+```
+
+Remove `--check-only` only for an authorized dispatch. `feature`, `bugfix` and
+`release` normally require a fresh successful canonical develop fetch, a qualified exact
+integration SHA, and an accepted pinned release ancestor. The explicit provisional
+exception below permits feature/bugfix development before the first certified release;
+it does not apply to release branches. `hotfix` fetches main
+and additionally requires that exact main to be accepted and released at a pinned
+canonical immutable tag. Missing/deleted/moved tags fail closed. No feature or
+bugfix starts from cached main. No inferred acceptance from build success,
+branch name, historical live receipts or provisioning status.
+
+The owner, permanent registered path, common Git directory and canonical origin
+must match. Dirty tracked or untracked files block dispatch. Switches and merges use
+`--no-overwrite-ignore`, so incoming tracked paths cannot overwrite ignored owner
+files. A collision fails closed; owner-reviewed preservation/removal is separate. Explicit preserved
+custody must be documented and the checkout made clean by its owner before this
+implementation proceeds; it never stashes or overwrites dirty work. Ignored
+files require explicit preserved evidence before retirement. Open PRs, recovery
+dependencies and evidence dependencies must be explicitly empty. Prior active
+tasks block reuse both in policy and completed receipt history. A task identifier
+is never reused, even after retirement. Check-only receipts do not consume an ID.
+Execution creates `KIND/NN/unique-task` directly from the fetched full SHA in the
+same worker path. It never forces, resets or rebases any branch.
+
