+### Completion and integration
+
+Write an actual check output file and a small JSON reference containing its
+absolute `path` and `sha256`. Pass that reference to `ready`:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B scripts/offmenu-gitflow.py --repo WORKER_PATH --policy POLICY --evidence-dir RECEIPTS \
+  ready --worker 9 --start EXACT_START_RECEIPT --checks CHECK_OUTPUT_REFERENCE_JSON
+```
+
+This pins the exact task commit, start receipt digest and check output digest.
+Completion means `ready_for_Morgan_review`; it does not produce acceptance.
+Morgan must review an **immutable prepared integration candidate**, the exact
+source commit and the freshly fetched target SHA. Candidate preparation and
+conflict resolution are separate authorized work; this tool does not guess a
+merge or resolve conflicts. A candidate must contain both source and target
+history. A fast-forward candidate is supported as well as a separately prepared
+merge commit. Qualified evidence must cover the entire candidate, not only the
+worker diff. Morgan-controlled policy has exactly one verdict for that triple.
+
+After preserving readiness, an explicitly authorized owner checks out the local
+target line in the same permanent worker. Never override Git's other-worktree
+ownership refusal. The local target must equal the freshly fetched canonical SHA.
+
+```sh
+python3 -B scripts/offmenu-gitflow.py --repo WORKER_PATH --policy POLICY --evidence-dir RECEIPTS \
+  integrate --worker 9 --ready EXACT_READY_RECEIPT --line develop \
+  --candidate FULL_REVIEWED_CANDIDATE_SHA --check-only
+```
+
+Execution uses only `merge --ff-only FULL_SHA`. Exact candidate or task changes,
+wrong reviewers, unqualified candidates and target movement fail closed. Only
+hotfixes can use `--line main`; releases use promotion and ordinary changes go to
+develop. Update line qualification only after actual reviewed integration and
+canonical publication by Morgan's separately authorized process. No pushes,
+force pushes, Actions, deployments or account changes are implemented here.
+
+Policy must retain exceptions for workers **01–08**. Their migration/cached-main
+bases remain preserved; never silently relabel them as develop starts. Record a preserved exception with
+`exception --worker N --task EXISTING_TASK` under explicit Matt/Morgan authorization
+and active-task custody. This does not fetch, create or switch a branch; it writes
+a completed start receipt labeled `unqualified-base-exception`, with
+`base_line: preserved-exception`. Pass that receipt to `ready`. The exception
+policy entry must pin `branch`, full `base`, `task`, `kind` (feature/bugfix only),
+`authorization` (Matt/Morgan), and an `evidence` file reference. This path also
+records the explicitly authorized Worker09 foundation exception. It does not
+qualify develop, release or integration. Before
+integration, if the current develop is not an ancestor of the immutable source,
+Morgan must supply a qualified reconciliation pinned to both the source and the
+new develop SHA. Any later develop advance invalidates that reconciliation.
+This applies to old base exceptions, releases and hotfix back-merges too.
+
+### Persistent develop, releases and hotfixes
+
+`initialize --worker 9 [--check-only]` is a one-time local proposal gated by a
+fresh main fetch equal to the accepted release, a canonical pinned accepted tag,
+an explicit Morgan `initialize-develop` verdict, explicit
+`develop_initialized: false`, and proven remote/local/tracking absence of develop.
+It creates a local branch only, without switching or pushing. Preserve the
+completed initialization receipt and set `develop_initialized: true` under
+Morgan custody before publishing develop. Never recreate develop each release,
+never clear initialization history to recover a deleted line. Recover that line
+through Morgan review. **Do not repeat real initialization:** Morgan has enacted the persistent line
+under the explicit provisional bootstrap above. Its release qualification remains
+unqualified; this command does not re-seed or certify that line.
+
+Release branches start from qualified freshly fetched develop. Reviewed release
+fixes must return to qualified canonical develop before main promotion. Use
+`integrate --line develop` with exact candidate and reconciliation as needed.
+Then Morgan's `promote-release` verdict must match candidate, fresh main base,
+and current qualified develop SHA. Promotion requires a completed release start
+receipt, exact release branch SHA, ancestry from the start base and released main,
+and candidate ancestry in develop. It requires main explicitly checked out at the
+fresh main SHA. The tag must be new both locally and on canonical origin.
+
+```sh
+python3 -B scripts/offmenu-gitflow.py --repo WORKER_PATH --policy POLICY --evidence-dir RECEIPTS \
+  promote --worker 9 --start EXACT_RELEASE_START_RECEIPT \
+  --candidate FULL_ACCEPTED_RELEASE_SHA --tag v1.2.0 --check-only
+```
+
+Execution fast-forwards local main and creates an annotated tag without force.
+No tag overwrite or remote publication exists in this script. Main/tag are two
+Git operations: if tag creation fails after main advances, the blocked receipt
+records `main_promoted`; preserve that state and ask Morgan to review recovery.
+There is no automatic rollback/reset. Morgan must preserve the acceptance verdict,
+qualification checks and tag object, publish through the authorized process, and
+update the released-main/line records before the next hotfix or release.
+
+Hotfixes start from fresh accepted/released main, require exact Morgan integration
+review, and return to **both main and develop** with reviewed candidates. Hotfix
+release/tag qualification remains Morgan-owned; this script's `promote` is for
+release branches. A hotfix cannot retire while absent from either canonical line.
+
+### Retirement
+
+```sh
+python3 -B scripts/offmenu-gitflow.py --repo WORKER_PATH --policy POLICY --evidence-dir RECEIPTS \
+  retire --worker 9 --start EXACT_START_RECEIPT --ready EXACT_READY_RECEIPT \
+  --integration EXACT_COMPLETED_INTEGRATION_RECEIPT --check-only
+```
+
+Requires unchanged task SHA; correct owner/active task; start, ready, checks and
+integration custody; exact Morgan integration verdict; source and integration
+candidate ancestry in qualified freshly fetched develop; both lines for release
+and hotfix; explicit preserved ignored-file inventory; no dirty/untracked files,
+open PRs or recovery/evidence dependencies; and an exact Morgan retirement verdict.
+Branches owned by another registered worktree are refused. Execution may detach
+this worker to the proven integration SHA, then deletes **only the named task
+branch** with `branch -d`. The permanent worker path is never removed. A completed
+retirement receipt must be preserved before clearing the active task record.
+
+PR retirement is a manual Morgan action after this evidence gate; the script has
+no provider API and cannot close/delete PRs. Its `open_prs` and ownership inventory
+are explicit, current Morgan custody attestations, not live GitHub API queries.
+There is no blanket cleanup, worktree removal, ref pruning, reset or branch reuse.
+
+## Policy contract and trust
+
+Policy is an explicit Morgan-controlled local record, **not a cryptographic
+identity system or server branch protection**. It must be reviewed and protected
+by existing custody. The script checks exact values and evidence byte hashes; it
+cannot prove an author called Morgan actually authored a hand-edited JSON file,
+that declared checks were sufficient, or that a PR inventory is truthful. Direct
+Git commands can bypass it. This is managed-command enforcement only; server
+protection, permissions and approval policy remain outside this scope.
+
+Every verdict has `reviewer: "Morgan"`, `verdict: "accepted"`,
+`qualification: "qualified"`, a valid non-future UTC `utc`, exact fields described
+below, and `evidence: {"path": "/absolute/receipt", "sha256": "FULL_SHA256"}`.
+No command self-accepts or writes policy. Do not use the placeholders below as
+qualification; fill them only from actual Morgan verdicts and preserved evidence.
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": "offmenu-gitflow-policy/1",
+  "pool_limit": 32,
+  "common_dir": "/home/user/src/offmenu/.git",
+  "origin": "git@github.com:maldous/offmenu.git",
+  "evidence_dir": "/absolute/retained/receipts",
+  "develop_initialized": false,
+  "baseline": {},
+  "released_main": {},
+  "lines": {},
+  "workers": {
+    "9": {
+      "path": "/home/user/src/offmenu-workers/worker-09",
+      "owner": "01a138ed-75f5-7511-af10-48685045d280",
+      "custody": "clear",
+      "evidence": {"path": "/absolute/custody-receipt", "sha256": "ACTUAL_HASH"},
+      "active_task": null,
+      "open_prs": [],
+      "recovery_dependencies": [],
+      "evidence_dependencies": []
+    }
+  },
+  "base_exceptions": {
+    "1": {"status": "preserved migration exception"},
+    "2": {"status": "preserved migration exception"},
+    "3": {"status": "preserved migration exception"},
+    "4": {"status": "preserved migration exception"},
+    "5": {"status": "preserved migration exception"},
+    "6": {"status": "preserved migration exception"},
+    "7": {"status": "preserved cached-main exception"},
+    "8": {"status": "preserved cached-main exception"}
+  },
+  "reviews": [],
+  "reconciliations": []
+}
+```
+
+For `baseline` and `released_main`, add verdict fields, exact `sha`, `tag` and
+`tag_object` (full tag object ID, including an annotated tag's separate object).
+Local tag commit and canonical remote object/peeled commit must match. Each
+`lines.develop`/`lines.main` entry is a verdict with `line` and exact `sha`.
+`reviews` entries use `operation`, `candidate`, `base`, `source`: operations are
+`initialize-develop`, `integrate-develop`, `integrate-main`, or `promote-release`.
+Initialization uses baseline for all three SHA fields; release promotion uses
+current develop as source. `reconciliations` entries use `source` and `develop`.
+Workers retiring tasks additionally need `ignored_custody: "preserved"`, an
+`ignored_evidence` file reference and `retirement` verdict with `source` and `task`.
+
+The existing deliverable ledger remains the assignment/review record:
+`/home/user/Documents/Codex/2026-10-14/task-2/offmenu-deliverable-ledger.json`.
+Gate policy/receipts complement it; workers may update only their own result/check
+receipt entry. Workers do not accept their own changes, edit other assignments,
+clear dependencies or invent missing baseline qualification. Source corpora stay
+referenced at their existing roots and are never copied by this tooling.
